oning Association","sourceKind":"professional_standard","evidenceQuality":88,"claims":["Use an intact appropriate loop band, clear level non-slip travel lane, adequate lateral clearance, footwear or bare-foot policy appropriate to the facility, a way to stop/exit, and communication. Selection is based on exact task and workout inputs, not a card-level population label."]},{"sectionKey":"dosage","sourceUrl":"https://www.nsca.com/globalassets/about/position-statements/position_stand_youth_resistance_training---2009.pdf","sourceTitle":"Youth Resistance Training: Updated Position Statement Paper From the NSCA","sourcePublisher":"National Strength and Conditioning Association","sourceKind":"professional_standard","evidenceQuality":88,"claims":["No universal step count, band tension, band placement, rest, preparation effect, or readiness threshold is established. Use a conservative quality-limited candidate dose, not a fatigue burn set, and stop before symptoms or uncorrectable loss of the specified cycle."]},{"sectionKey":"instructions","sourceUrl":"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC5847412/","sourceTitle":"Elastic Resistance Effectiveness on Increasing Strength of Shoulders and Hips","sourcePublisher":"Journal of Strength and Conditioning Research","sourceKind":"peer_reviewed_research","evidenceQuality":88,"claims":["Instructions must name the above-knee loop band, athletic stance, small lateral lead step, controlled trailing-foot follow, maintained tension, direction change, and reset. Do not infer a required squat depth, toe angle, step width, or band color."]},{"sectionKey":"safety_stop_rules","sourceUrl":"https://www.nsca.com/globalassets/about/position-statements/position_stand_youth_resistance_training---2009.pdf","sourceTitle":"Youth Resistance Training: Updated Position Statement Paper From the NSCA","sourcePublisher":"National Strength and Conditioning Association","sourceKind":"professional_standard","evidenceQuality":88,"claims":["Appropriate instructi